WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-Our next guest
is an award-winning

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.734
and Michelin-starred chef.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:07.200
You can catch him in L.A.
December 1st, 2nd, and 3rd

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.701
for ChainFest, the world's first
chain-food festival.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.434
Please welcome chef
Tim Hollingsworth.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:14.834
Hey!
-What's up, everybody?

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.701
Thank you, thank you, thank you.
-Time, nice to see you bud.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.300
Welcome.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.801
-Tariq.
-Good to be here.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.767
-Chef, can you explain
what ChainFest is?

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.167
What inspired it?
-I mean, we throw

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:29.434
massive, 300-person
dinner parties back in L.A.,

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:33.934
where we focus on making iconic
chain dishes in a gourmet way.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.667
-Now, can you walk us
through some of these things?

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.734
Tell me about
these things tonight.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.200
What is this one over here?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.467
-This right here is the the
Chili's babyback rib-wich.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:47.634
So we have a $3,000 bottle
of Pappy Van Winkle

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:50.300
that went into that
barbecue sauce as glazing.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.767
We also have these Wagyu beef,

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:58.200
iconic Jack in the Box
tacos with the curly fries.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.133
-Oh, my God.
-And we have sweet-and-sour

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.667
Pepsi sauce.
-You're elevating this.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.801
You're upcycling these dishes.
-Upcycling.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:04.801
[ Laughter ]
-That's not a --

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:08.567
It's not a popular term.
-I mean...

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.834
-Dunkin'.
All right.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.133
So what are you doing
with Dunkin'?

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.634
-Dunkin' Donuts?
We have three different versions

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.567
of doughnuts here.
We have a creme brulee doughnut,

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.334
we have a bacon doughnut,
and we've taken

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.267
the iconic strawberry doughnut,

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.767
and we turned it
into a drink here.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.234
So it's espresso and strawberry
with sprinkle on it doughnut.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.067
-Cold brew?
-Yes.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.667
-And then Red Robin.
What'd you do here?

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.133
-Last but not least,
yes, Red Robin.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.400
We have -- They're famous
for their burgers, right?

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.167
So we have a burgertini
with a savory beef broth.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.767
-Oh, wow.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.634
-I mean...
-Yeah. Not bad.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.767
I don't understand what I
just drank, but it's great.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.567
-Wow.
-That's actually not --

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:45.801
I love that.
That's not bad.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.334
I figured that, tonight,
in honor of ChainFest,

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.601
we'd do something fun.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.534
It's time for "The Tonight Show
Chain Challenge."

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.667
-Oh, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.767
-♪ Tonight Show ♪

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:56.901
-♪ Tonight Show
Chain Challenge ♪

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:59.267
♪ Yeah, yeah ♪

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:01.567
-All right,
here's how this works.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.434
Tariq and I will have 45 seconds

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.534
to create our own
original menu items

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.300
using existing
chain-restaurant foods.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.467
We can use as many
chain-restaurant items

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.901
as we want, but we must
transform the dish

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:14.100
into something new.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.834
We also have access
to the pantry.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:20.234
Chef Tim will take a bite
of each finished dish

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.667
and determine the winner,

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.434
who will receive
"The Tonight Show"

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.467
Chain Championship Chain.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:29.200
Chain chain!

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.934
Put 45 seconds on the clock.
On your mark,

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.267
get set, go!

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.167
All right, here we go.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.033
Coming over.
All right.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.200
Here's what I'm doing.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.801
I'm gonna make
a Korean-style chicken sandwich.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.901
I'm putting nuggets in here.
Right?

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:46.434
Putting some gochujang, some
spicy Korean paste in there.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.567
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-That's good.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.734
Tariq, what do you got?
-I got a little chicken.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.367
I got a little...
-I got to put a little...

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:55.133
-...doughnut action there.
-A little soy sauce.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.934
-Chicken doughnut.
-Soy sauce in there.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.868
-The inspiration is --
-Soy sauce in there!

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:03.267
I'm putting a little --
little sesame oil in there.

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:07.033
-He's making chicken and waffle.
-A little sesame oil in there!

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.701
-Got chicken and waffles!
-I'm putting, uh, honey.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.767
I'm putting honey in there.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.400
I can't open this.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.000
Oh, yeah.
A little rice vinegar.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.234
Honey in there.
-Look at that, look at that.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.868
-How much time?
[ Ding! ]

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.868
-Pickles, chicken.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-All right, here we go.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:29.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.868
-All right. Tariq, knives down!
Tariq, don't --

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:36.467
No more.
Tariq, knives down, bud.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.434
Nice try.
There you go. Hands up!

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.767
All right, here we go.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.200
Time is up.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.000
Chef Tim.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.868
What I made for you tonight,
using Red Robin ingredients,

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:53.067
is a Korean-styled chicken
nugget chicken sandwich

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.634
with gochujang.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.734
Some sesame oil in there.
You got some rice vinegar.

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.067
You want a little honey
in there,

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.801
you get a little pickle taste
on that Red Robin bun.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.267
Look at this.
Wow. You should see --

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.067
Wow. Yeah.
Well, you can't complain

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.634
about that, right?
Come on. Yeah, respect.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.767
That's what I'm talking about.
-Sweet, sour, spicy.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.434
-Sweet, sour, spicy.
-I like the pickles.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:11.601
You took the breading off.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:12.968
-Yeah, I took the --
Yeah, I took -- yeah.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.067
Thank you.
Appreciate that.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.000
-So, in honor of the release
of my book, "The Upcycled Self,"

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.901
I've upcycled this chain food.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:24.067
And I took, you know,
two glazed doughnuts,

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.000
and I made
that my sandwich base.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.367
And I did something that's like
a spin on the classic

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.000
chicken and waffles.
I used, you know,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.767
the Chili's boneless wings.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.567
I added a little sriracha,
a little honey,

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:36.167
and a little pickle
to top it off.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.067
-Sounds like what I made
a little bit.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.367
-Oh, wow.
-And I also like you a lot, man.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:43.801
Like, I think -- I think
you're a pretty cool, dude.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.801
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.467
I appreciate it.
-It's been great having you.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:48.901
-I appreciate it, yeah.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.601
I mean, you --
you eat too much of that,

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.267
you're gonna upcycle
in the morning.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.367
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.834
Chef, there can only be
one winn--

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.367
There can only be one winner.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:05.234
Who gets "The Tonight Show"
Chain Chain?

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:08.067
-The winner of "Tonight Show"
Chain Challenge,

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.801
and the recipient
of "The Tonight Show"

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:13.033
Chain Championship Chain is...

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.067
...Tariq.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:20.801
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.701
-Oh-whee!

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:26.100
-Come on, now.
-It looks good on him.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.434
Look at that.

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.734
-Chef Tim Hollingsworth.
-Check out ChainFest in L.A.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.267
December 1st through the 3rd.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.234
We'll be right back.
More "Tonight Show."

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:34.801
Stick around, everybody.

